    {
      "detail": "A weight-5 error is the complement, inside a unique octad of the Steiner system S(5,8,24), of a weight-3 error, so the received word sits at distance 3 from the wrong codeword and 5 from the right one.  Every nearest-codeword rule is unique, confident and wrong here; the remedy is a declared channel radius, not a better decoder.  This is a null result for correction beyond the radius and is reported as one.",
      "key": "weight_5_is_confidently_wrong",
      "statement": "42504 of 42504 weight-5 patterns decode to a unique, wrong codeword."
    }
